  e2 [verified, public, as of 2026-04-06T00:00:00-06:00] A commitment is recorded on the board at the moment the grower makes it and is immediately visible to anyone who consults the board afterwards. The board displays the running total of committed pallets and nothing else -- no names, no pending intentions, no forecasts. (source: Co-op bulk-order rule 2)
  e3 [verified, public, as of 2026-04-06T00:00:00-06:00] Once the board closes at 5:00 PM Thursday, no further commitment can be recorded. The depot manager has no discretion to accept a late commitment and has never accepted one in the eleven years the board has run. (source: Co-op bulk-order rule 3; depot manager's statement)
  e4 [verified, public, as of 2026-04-06T00:00:00-06:00] A commitment, once recorded, cannot be withdrawn or reduced. No grower has asked to withdraw one for this order. (source: Co-op bulk-order rule 4; depot manager's statement)
  e5 [verified, public, as of 2026-04-10T00:00:00-06:00] Eight growers are eligible for this order. Each consults the board exactly once during the order period, at the time fixed for them by the co-op's binding rotation roster; each decides then and there and does not consult the board again. No grower has ever departed from the roster. (source: Co-op rotation roster for spring 2026; depot manager's statement)
  e6 [verified, public, as of 2026-04-10T00:00:00-06:00] The growers do not discuss the order with one another. Co-op bulk-order rule 6 forbids soliciting commitments off the board, and the depot manager confirms that no grower contacted another about this order. No grower has any information about the order beyond what the board showed at their own rostered slot. (source: Co-op bulk-order rule 6; depot manager's statement)
